{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Use case: stylized-concept. Create a Minecraft builder reference sheet, landscape 3:2, high resolution, plain light background, crisp vanilla Minecraft voxel blocks only, no characters or animals. Two views SIDE BY SIDE: LEFT straight-on front elevation, orthographic; RIGHT three-quarter view of the SAME COMPLETE eight-plot street at the SAME SCALE. Both views must show all eight plots, in the same left-to-right order, without cropping. Use the width of each panel for the long street; generous white space is fine. Skilled human builder quality: real massing, projecting porches, recessed framed openings, stepped block roofs with verges, eaves and ridges; sub-block stairs, slabs, fences, walls, trapdoors and lanterns. No smooth non-Minecraft architecture. Small plot numbers 0 through 7 beneath each view. Add a compact block-key footer naming principal materials by exact ids.\\nSite: sunny Mississippi cotton mill village about 1900. Exactly eight contiguous 12-block-wide plots, total 96 wide by 19 deep, 1–2 storeys except Queen Anne tower about 22 blocks high. Gravel-and-dirt lane across front. Different wood picket fences, each plot with centred gate, lantern posts every 12 blocks. Every house on brick or stone piers with raised porch.\\nLeft to right:\\n0 dusty-blue clapboard double shotgun, white trim, oxblood tin front-gable roof. Two adjacent doors and tall shuttered windows, gingerbread brackets supporting shared porch, twin brick chimney at back.\\n1 pink-board Creole cottage, one steep dark cypress-shingle roof sweeping over full-width galerie on slim dark posts. Two pairs French doors with green board shutters. Brick chimney on west gable.\\n2 square two-storey ochre American Foursquare, dark hipped roof with front dormer, white belt course, full-width porch on brick-pedestal columns, brick side chimney.\\n3 finest superintendent Queen Anne: plum clapboard ground storey, cream fishscale-effect upper storey built from staggered birch slabs/stairs. Front cross gable beside three-stage square corner tower, glazed belvedere and tall copper pyramid cap. Wraparound porch with turned-post effect and spindle frieze, orange stained glass over door.\\n4 blue-grey gable-front-and-wing farmhouse, weathered cedar-brown roofs, porch in L angle.\\n5 dark vertical-board mule barn, red gambrel roof and cupola, hayloft door with hoist beam; block-built wagon under east lean-to, small fenced rear paddock.\\n6 gravel yard: open green-tin picnic pavilion on SIX log posts over long table, domed stepped brick bread oven with smoking stack, wooden water tank on braced legs and rain barrels underneath.\\n7 red-brick company duplex, stone sills and cornice, two adjacent front doors, two-storey porch on brick piers with upper gallery, low grey hipped roof, two rear brick chimneys.\\nStrict allowed palette by role (exact Minecraft ids; choose these to approximate historic materials):\\nground: grass_block, coarse_dirt, podzol, rooted_dirt, dirt_path, gravel, packed_mud, stone, dirt.\\nfoundation: bricks, brick_stairs, brick_slab, brick_wall, stone_bricks, mossy_stone_bricks, stone_brick_stairs, stone_brick_slab, stone_brick_wall, cobblestone, mossy_cobblestone, cobblestone_wall, cobbled_deepslate, cobbled_deepslate_stairs, cobbled_deepslate_slab, deepslate_bricks.\\ndecks_floors: dark_oak_planks, dark_oak_slab, dark_oak_stairs, jungle_planks, jungle_slab, spruce_planks, spruce_slab, spruce_stairs.\\nwalls: light_blue_terracotta, cherry_planks, cherry_slab, yellow_terracotta, crimson_planks, birch_planks, cyan_terracotta, stripped_dark_oak_log, stripped_spruce_log, stripped_oak_log, stripped_spruce_wood.\\ntrim: stripped_birch_log, stripped_birch_wood, birch_slab, birch_stairs, smooth_stone_slab, polished_andesite_slab, smooth_quartz, smooth_quartz_slab, smooth_quartz_stairs.\\nroof: red_nether_bricks, red_nether_brick_stairs, red_nether_brick_slab, neth